\section{Codex Volume Structure}
Each Codex volume follows the structure:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item \textbf{Volume Header}
    \item \textbf{Subsystem Overview}
    \item \textbf{Mathematical Operators}
    \item \textbf{Update Equations}
    \item \textbf{Stress Envelope}
    \item \textbf{Glyph Seals}
    \item \textbf{Sovereign Closure}
\end{enumerate}

\section{Codex Integration}
Volumes are designed to be independent but composable. The unified Codex spine
is defined by:
\[
\mathcal{C}_{\text{SAIE-X}} =
\bigcup_{i=1}^{N} V_i,
\]
where $V_i$ are individual Codex volumes.

